<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
  App icon: what the app actually is - one remote picture, a pointer we send back
  into it, and the three protocols that can feed that picture.

  The monitor is one path with the screen as a second subpath filled evenOdd, so the
  screen is a real hole rather than white paint: as a themed (single colour) icon the
  frame still reads as a display instead of a solid block. The three capsules below are
  GameStream, VNC and ADB, in the accent gold, the mini window blue and a dark gray.
  The background is transparent on purpose, which rules out an adaptive icon: the
  framework paints its layers onto opaque black. The launcher therefore uses the
  rasterised copies in mipmap-*, both generated from the same geometry by
  _icon_connect_gen_e1.ps1 - edit that script, never these files.
-->
